HST Office: DURATION and MDURATION with the actual/actual basis, ODDFPRICE and ODDFYIELD as in the leading
spreadsheet application (owner 18/11: in 1.0.3). Before, DURATION(DATE(2018,7,1),DATE(2048,1,1),0.08,0.09,2,1)
gave 10.92157 (its vendor documents 10.9191453), MDURATION with basis 1 5.73392 (5.73567), and ODDFPRICE and
ODDFYIELD were always #VALUE! (the algorithm was disabled upstream).

Written clean-room from the vendor's public function documentation and general bond mathematics, without
reading LibreOffice's implementation of these functions: sc analysis add-in
scaddins/source/analysis/hstbondfunctions.cxx (SPDX LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary). Coupon schedule stepped back
from maturity (DURATION) or from the first coupon (the odd period), day counts per basis 0-4; DURATION is the
Macaulay duration over the coupons after settlement, MDURATION divides it by 1+yld/frequency; ODDFPRICE covers
the short and the long odd first coupon period with the vendor's variables (NC, Nq, DCi, NLi, Ai, DSC, E, N);
ODDFYIELD solves ODDFPRICE for the yield (Newton steps in a bracket, bisection fallback). Domain errors are
#NUM! (frequency, basis, negative rate or yield, date order). Hooks: the four add-in entry points in
financial.cxx call it.

Test: CppunitTest_sc_hst_bond_functions (the vendor's examples: DURATION 10.9191453, MDURATION 5.73567,
ODDFPRICE 113.597717, ODDFYIELD 7.72%; long first coupon prices with the yield round trip; #NUM! cases).
